'''Ben Tey Dogon''', named after the village ''Been'' it is spoken in, is a divergent, recently described [[Dogon language]] spoken in [[Mali]]. It is closely related to [[Bankan Tey Dogon|Bankan Tey]] and [[Nanga Dogon|Nanga]] Dogon. It is said that elders in the Dogon village of ''Gawru'' also speak this language. Been is reported to have been settled from the village of Walo, and Ben Tey Dogon differs from [[Walo Dogon]] primarily from being under a different foreign influence, as Been village is surrounded by [[Jamsay Dogon|Jamsay]]-speaking villages, which Walo is not.

